      "page_title": "Moves: Assignment & Bit Copies",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Borrow Ends At Last Use"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "NLL since 2018",
          "text": "A borrow now ends at its last use, not at the closing brace. Errors are narrower than the old lexical rules taught."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Assignment Moves",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let a = String::from(\"x\");",
            "let b = a;         // a moved into b",
            "println!(\"{a}\");   // E0382, a is dead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Source binding invalidated — compiler marks it moved out",
            "Only one of the two ever runs drop, so no double free",
            "Move of a non-Copy value is the default, not the exception"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The Error You Will See",
          "items": [
            "`error[E0382]: borrow of moved value: `a``",
            "note: `a` has type `String`",
            "which does not implement the `Copy` trait"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Actually Copies"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "spec": {
            "rows": [
              [
                "a.ptr",
                "a.len"
              ],
              [
                "b.ptr",
                "b.len"
              ],
              [
                "one heap buffer"
              ]
            ],
            "highlight": [],
            "caption": "memcpy of header only"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The 3-word header is memcpy'd, nothing more",
            "Heap buffer is NOT duplicated — moves are cheap",
            "The optimizer elides most moves entirely",
            "No move-constructor hook: always a plain bit copy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "No Self-Reference",
          "text": "A value may not point into itself, because a move relocates the bytes. That is exactly why `Pin` exists for futures."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Deep Copy On Demand"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
